# Production build defaults. `vite build` loads this file; `vite` (dev) and
# Vitest do not — so local development never pollutes production analytics.
#
# Everything in here is public by design: GA measurement IDs and Clarity
# project IDs ship to every visitor's browser inside the bundle. Committing
# them means a deploy can't quietly lose analytics because nobody re-entered
# them in the Vercel dashboard. Real environment variables still win, so the
# dashboard can override any of these.
#
# Forking this repo? Swap in your own IDs, or you'll be measuring your traffic
# into someone else's dashboards. (Analytics only ever run after a visitor
# accepts the consent banner.)
VITE_GA_TRACKING_ID=G-1K72061LE9
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=vkvf3nb96r

# Sentry DSN for error reports, public by design like the IDs above. Two rules:
#   1. It belongs to the project that receives the source maps, i.e. the one
#      SENTRY_ORG / SENTRY_PROJECT name in Vercel (andres-suarez-dev/portfolio).
#      Until September 2026 it pointed at a project in another org, and not
#      one alert ever arrived.
#   2. vercel.json's CSP report endpoint and script-src follow it. A test checks.
# Change it here rather than in the Vercel dashboard, so that test can see it.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://b47e937f8c43e8a7a79c656bb09b27f9@o4510980468572160.ingest.us.sentry.io/4510980472438784
